---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Freightgcc"
  description="What Freightgcc processes when you read a page or email the desk: server logs, correspondence, the legal basis for each, retention, sharing, your rights."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Last reviewed 15 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Freightgcc is a static editorial site. It has no accounts, no forms, no newsletter, no comments
      and no analytics script. That removes most of the data a typical publisher collects — but not all
      of it. This page states exactly what remains, why it is processed, how long it is kept, and what
      you can require us to do with it.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
    <p>
      The operator of Freightgcc is the data controller for the processing described here. Contact for
      any privacy question or request:
      <a href="mailto:admin@freightgcc.com">admin@freightgcc.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site does not currently publish a company registration number or a postal address; that
      position is stated on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> rather than filled with a
      placeholder. If a legal entity is established, its name and address will be added here and to the
      contact page before any other change is made.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What is processed, and why</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Category</th><th>When</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Server logs: IP address, user agent, requested URL, referrer, timestamp, response status</td>
            <td>Every request, generated by the hosting and CDN provider</td>
            <td>Deliver pages, keep the service available, detect and block abuse</td>
            <td>Legitimate interest in operating a secure service</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Email address and message content</td>
            <td>When you write to the editorial desk</td>
            <td>Answer the question, investigate a correction, keep a correspondence trail</td>
            <td>Legitimate interest; consent where you volunteer sensitive detail</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Any personal detail you choose to include in that email</td>
            <td>At your discretion</td>
            <td>Understand and answer the question</td>
            <td>Consent, withdrawable at any time</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      No account data, payment data, advertising identifiers, precise location, contact lists or
      cross-site tracking data are collected, because none of those features exist on the site.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What is not collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No analytics or measurement script (no Google Analytics, no Matomo, no Plausible).</li>
      <li>No advertising or retargeting pixel, and no advertising identifiers.</li>
      <li>No session recording, heatmap or A/B testing tool.</li>
      <li>No account, login, comment, newsletter or contact form — email is the only channel.</li>
      <li>No data is sold, rented or shared with data brokers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      The site sets no cookies of its own. The hosting provider may set a short-lived security cookie
      to distinguish browsers from automated traffic; it is essential to serving the site and is not
      used for profiling. The full position, including how to block it, is on the
      <a href="/cookies/">cookie page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Retention</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Retention</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Server logs</td>
            <td>The short operational window configured at the hosting and CDN provider; not exported or archived by Freightgcc</td>
            <td>Security and availability; there is no editorial use for them</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Editorial correspondence</td>
            <td>Up to 24 months from the last message, then deleted</td>
            <td>So that a correction or a query can be traced</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Published corrections</td>
            <td>Retained indefinitely in the public log</td>
            <td>Accuracy and accountability; personal data is included only with consent</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>6. Who receives data</h2>
    <p>
      Data is shared only with the providers needed to run the site: the static hosting and CDN
      provider, and the email provider that receives editorial mail. Those providers process data on
      documented instructions and under their own standard terms. No other recipient is authorised.
    </p>
    <p>
      A provider may process data outside your country. Where that happens, the transfer relies on the
      provider's standard contractual clauses or an equivalent safeguard, and only the minimum data
      needed to deliver the service is transferred.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over HTTPS with HSTS enabled and a content security policy. It runs as static
      files: there is no application database, no login system and no stored user content to breach.
      Access to the publishing repository and the editorial mailbox is limited to the operator and
      protected by multi-factor authentication.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Right</th><th>What it means here</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Access</td><td>Ask what personal data is held about you — in practice, correspondence and any log entry that can still be linked to you.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rectification</td><td>Ask for an inaccurate email record to be corrected.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Erasure</td><td>Ask for correspondence to be deleted, subject to the need to keep a correction trail.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Restriction</td><td>Ask that correspondence be kept but not used while a dispute is resolved.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Objection</td><td>Object to processing based on legitimate interest; the request is balanced against the security need.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Portability</td><td>Ask for correspondence you supplied in a machine-readable format.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Withdraw consent</td><td>Where processing relies on consent, withdraw it at any time without affecting prior processing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Complain</td><td>Lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority in your country of residence or work.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Requests are answered within 30 days. Identity may need to be verified where the request concerns
      correspondence; no fee is charged for a first request.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The site is written for a professional audience and is not directed at children. It does not
      knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 16.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      Material changes are dated at the top of this page and, where they affect what is collected or
      why, are also recorded on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. The previous version
      remains in the repository history.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Related</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/cookies/">Cookie policy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms of use</a> ·
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a> ·
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
